  "what": "problem PD-1@v2 drafted",
  "phase": "DEFINE",
  "minute": 119.0,
  "event_seq": 286,
  "root_problem": "Dispute ticket volume roughly doubled from a ~600/month baseline to 1180-1260/month starting August 2026 (E-07). Of the 1240 disputed ESTIMATED-read bills (vs 1785 ACTUAL-read, E-02), 1184 trace to AMI reads delivered on time but rejected at billing import with status REJECTED_HIGH_CONSUMPTION (E-12). This traces to billing import validation rule BV-17, deployed 2026-08-01, which compares raw AMI register values directly against 12-month m3 consumption history with unit_scaling=none (E-13); because firmware v4.2 meters (rollout 2026-06) report raw register values in units of 0.1 m3 while legacy v3.x meters report in whole m3 (E-14), BV-17's unscaled comparison misclassifies normal v4.2 consumption as anomalously high and rejects it at import, forcing estimate substitution that triggers disputes. This mechanism accounts for the ESTIMATED-read subset; the larger ACTUAL-read dispute majority (1785) is not yet explained by it."
 },
